# ACF/WST Patterns

Use this Rule when writing or reviewing WST Builder work for Section templates, ACF section field groups, Flexible Content layouts, clone child fields, WST shortcodes, or `flexible-content.php` registrations.

## Required Context

Before changing WST or ACF structure, read the project-local context for:

- WST template paths and the active `flexible-content.php` registration point.
- Flexible Content field key and field post ID.
- Standard clone group keys for content, button, and layout.
- Existing Section templates and ACF field group patterns.
- Section handoff location and target dev or staging URL.

Do not invent real field keys, field post IDs, clone group keys, layout keys, page IDs, URLs, theme values, access details, or client examples. Use placeholders such as `<fc-field-key>`, `<fc-post-id>`, `<section-field-group-key>`, `<layout-key>`, and `<staging-url>` until Project Context supplies the real values.

## Flexible Content Invariants

- Every reusable Section layout has a Flexible Content layout entry, one clone child field under the Flexible Content field post, and one Section field group cloned by that child field.
- The clone child field's `parent_layout` must exactly match the generated Flexible Content layout key.
- Layout names should follow the project pattern, usually `layout_<section_slug_with_underscores>`.
- Section field groups should keep shared content, button, and layout fields as clones, with Section-specific fields added separately.
- Cloned fields with `prefix_name: 1` change the saved meta key shape; account for that when reviewing shortcode field names.
- Resolve the page Flexible Content field through the field group assigned to post type `page`, not by the bare name `flexible_content`; several fields share that name (page builder, flexblocks, multi-column).
- Expanded clone field names are the storage and resolution truth: with `prefix_name=1`, a `title` field cloned through `content` into layout `intro` resolves and stores as `intro_content_title`. Programmatic writes and preview fixtures use the expanded names.

## WST Template Invariants

- Guard PHP templates with `if (! defined('ABSPATH')) exit;`.
- Preserve project placeholders such as `{{conditional_logic_start}}` and `{{conditional_logic_end}}` when existing templates use them.
- Use a stable primary Section class such as `.wso-section-<section-slug>`.
- Keep WST row, wrap, column, and column-attribute classes consistent with nearby templates.
- Register the template include with the matching layout name in the Flexible Content render block.
- Output filled WYSIWYG title/subline fields with `[wst_acf field='...' format_value='0']` so `wpautop` does not wrap `<p>` inside headings. `[wst_acf_wysiwyg]` returns empty in Flexible Content loop context; do not use it for FC sub-fields.

## Programmatic Writes And QA Invariants

- Write Flexible Content programmatically with `update_field(<fc-field-key>, $rows, $post_id)` using expanded clone names. This keeps the ACFE performance blob consistent; direct `update_post_meta` or SQL writes do not update the blob, and hybrid reads prefer the blob.
- A full Flexible Content rewrite does not delete foreign native metas at reused row indexes. After index-shifting rewrites, diff native metas per row against the expected field set and clean the strays (dry-run the deletion list first).
- Never anchor structural QA checks on HTML comments; minifiers strip them from the served output. Use real tags or `data-` attributes, and scope checks to the target Section chunk because global template instances can render the same Section a second time.

See `acf-wst-patterns-reference.md` for the `update_field` shape, the stale-meta caveat, the migration safety net, ACFE hybrid mode, autop details, virtual-route hooks, and QA fetch pitfalls.

## PHP Bootstrap Safety

Do not edit `functions.php`. It is forbidden for agent edits even when the child theme is otherwise inside the project-approved editable path.

Edit `theme-functions.php` only after explicit prior user confirmation for the exact change. Edit or create MU plugin files only after explicit prior user confirmation for the exact change.

## Scope Boundary

This Rule owns reusable WST Builder structure and review checks. Final visual CSS, new Section CSS files, style loader registration, responsive QA, Chrome Local Overrides spikes, local Playwright MCP browser QA, and optional project-local Playwright regression checks belong to Frontend Design QA. WordPress server access, cache policy, media import, and access setup belong to WordPress Server Ops or Project Context.

The `wst-section-workflow` Skill owns the Section workflow itself, including work-type classification, the preflight write-gate, existing-section remodel protections, and live or unknown environment write confirmations.

See `acf-wst-patterns-reference.md` for shortcode tables, template examples, field shape details, and post-meta notes.
